Hi,
yes, you described the issue well, it's because PHPStan sees the types like this:

```php
class HelloWorld
{
	public function toArray($value): array
	{
		// mixed
		if (is_array($value)) {
			// array
			return $value;
		}

		// mixed
		
		if (is_iterable($value)) {
			// intersection of mixed and iterable is iterable
			return iterator_to_array($value);
		}

		// mixed
		
		throw new \LogicException();
	}
}
```

That's because a feature called "complement types" that would do exactly what you described, isn't yet implemented.

You have  two ways of fixing this: Either change the second `if` to `$value instanceof Traversable` (https://phpstan.org/r/04243cb2301902f5946c886fb8afb764) or add a typehint to the method (https://phpstan.org/r/61b806fa2cbe7e8c3e29ea9052cd10a8):


```php
public function toArray(iterable $value): array
```

If you're at least on level 5, you can them simplify the method body like this:

```php
class HelloWorld
{

	public function toArray(iterable $value): array
	{
		if (is_array($value)) {
			return $value;
		}

		return iterator_to_array($value);
	}
}
```

Because PHPStan checks that nothing else actually get passed to the method (even when the type is just in phpDoc) 😊

or if you want to preserve mixed parameter
```php
class HelloWorld
{
    public function toArray($value): array
    {
        if (!is_iterable($value))
        {
            throw new \LogicException();
        }

        if (is_array($value))
        {
            return $value;
        }

        if (is_iterable($value)) // unecessary
        {
            return iterator_to_array($value);
        }
    }
}
```

